# Databases are build outputs. `python scripts/build_seed_db.py` regenerates
# data/seed.db from data/library_loans.csv in about a second, so committing it
# would mean carrying a 2 MB binary in every diff for no reason. Commit the
# code and the source data that produce the database, never the database.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/seed.db

# NOT ignored, deliberately, and do not "clean this up":
#   data/library_loans.csv       the 20,000-row source extract
#   data/refresh_state.json      what the last pipeline run found
# A template that ships with no data is a template nobody can start. If you add
# a rule here that matches data/*.csv, a stranger clones this repo and the first
# command in the README fails.

# Secrets. A real secret in git HISTORY is an automatic fail on the Portfolio
# Factory rubric, and deleting the file in a later commit does not remove it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
